    "skyPreset": "golden_alpine_meadow",
    "loreSummary": "Limepot is the one surveyed region on Stonemoor with neither a village on it nor a road across it, and it is a sheet of bare split rock from end to end. Parties come up onto it for two things and go straight back down: block stone levered out of the pavement along the run of the beds, and ore off the two limestone towers standing in it, worked from the outside in daylight instead of from a shaft."
  },
